#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inverse_z_transform

#% text
# `inverse_z_transform(F, z, n)` gives the sequence whose Z transform is `F`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A rational function of `z` is inverted by the residues of `F(z) z^(n - 1)` at its nonzero poles; a pole at 0 gives `discrete_delta(n - j)` terms.

#% item
# The inverse of a `z_transform` of an undefined function is the function.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z/(z - a), z, n)
#% output
#= a^n

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z/(z - 1)^2, z, n)
#% output
#= n

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(1/z^3, z, n)
#% output
#= discrete_delta(-3 + n)

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z/((z - 1)*(z - 2)), z, n)
#% output
#= -1 + 2^n

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z/(z^2 + 1), z, n)
#% output
#= -im/2*im^n + (im/2)*(-im)^n

#% text
# A pole of order 3 and a pole at a point other than 1:

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z/(z - 1)^3, z, n)
#% output
#= (1/2)*n*(-1 + n)

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(1/(z - 2), z, n)
#% output
#= (1/2)*(-discrete_delta(n) + 2^n)

#% text
# Complex conjugate poles, and the Fibonacci-type recurrence:

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z/(z^2 - 2*z + 2), z, n)
#% output
#= -im/2*(1 + im)^n + (im/2)*(1 - im)^n

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z^2/(z^2 - z - 1), z, n)
#% output
#= (-1/5)*(-(1/2 + (1/2)*5^(1/2))^(1 + n) + (1/2 - (1/2)*5^(1/2))^(1 + n))*5^(1/2)

#% text
# A power series in `1/z` after a rational cancellation:

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(1/(1 - 1/(2*z)), z, n)
#% output
#= (1/2)^n

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# A number for `n` gives the value there:

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z/(z - 2), z, 5)
#% output
#= 32

#% text
# `assumptions:` and `generate_conditions:` are accepted; the region of convergence is not reported by the inverse:

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z/(z - a), z, n, assumptions: abs(a) < 1)
#% output
#= a^n

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z/(z - a), z, n, generate_conditions: true)
#% output
#= a^n

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The transform of the result gives `F` back:

#% cell
simplify(z_transform(inverse_z_transform(z^2/((z - 1)*(z - 2)), z, n), n, z))
#% output
#= z^2/(2 - 3*z + z^2)

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A function that is not rational in `z` is inverted when its series in `1/z` is known; one that is not stays a call:

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(exp(1/z), z, n)
#% output
#= factorial(n)^-1

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(sin(1/z), z, n)
#% output
#= inverse_z_transform(sin(z^-1), z, n)

#% text
# `z` and `z^2` give sequences that are not zero at negative `n`, written with `discrete_delta`:

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z^2, z, n)
#% output
#= discrete_delta(2 + n)

#% text
# An undefined function stays a call:

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(F(z), z, n)
#% output
#= inverse_z_transform(F(z), z, n)

#% text
# A number for `n` at the precision wanted gives the value at that precision (there is no `working_precision:`):

#% cell
inverse_z_transform(z/(z - 2), z, n(5, 30))
#% output
#= 32.000000000000000000000000000000000

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `z_transform`, `inverse_laplace_transform`, `apart`
